The XML and meshes were vendored from the user's existing dual-arm-sort
internship project. Its upstream commit was not recorded. The inherited XML
contains local contact, end-effector site, and wrist-camera configuration
changes. It should not be represented as an unmodified current upstream XML.

The conveyor project additionally constructs a runtime scene in model.py that
namespaces two copies, places their bases, changes actuator parameters, and
removes unused wrist-camera configuration. It replaces the inherited five
overlapping fingertip collision boxes with one flat contact pad per finger
inside the same outer envelope, and calibrates finger contact friction to
1.0 / 0.015 / 0.001. This avoids a small collision-geometry ledge that trapped
round objects after the gripper opened. Visual meshes and mesh geometry are
unchanged; these primitive collision changes occur only in the runtime model.

Version 0.6 optionally generates new wrist-camera housings, lenses, brackets,
and calibrated cameras at runtime. These sensor fixtures are visual-only,
without added mass or collision geometry, and do not alter the Panda meshes.

